question 2E30 EXOS 8 at $2E36 writes 10 bytes from $2F3E, but $2F44 is code (a JR target, $2F55): are only 6 meant, or do 4 code bytes go out too?
question 3E7A $3E7A-$3E7F (dec hl, push hl, ld c,$FF, inc hl, ld a,(hl)) runs into the $FF fill and nothing reaches it: a cut-off routine?

feedback pattern 00F2-00F2 Every call to $00F2 (28 of them) is followed by one inline byte; only the 13 read in the profile were proposed, and inline bytes swallowed code at $0383, $03B7, $0A00, $0F32, $16DA, $19B3. A callee that does ex (sp),hl / ld e,(hl) / inc hl / ex (sp),hl should mark the byte after every call
feedback missing 0550-058D ld hl,$C550 / add hl,bc / ld e,(hl) at $0524 indexes a 31-entry word table (cp $1F at $0505); the proposals offered five fragments ($0552, $0558, $0568, $057A, $058F) and false targets ($38D7, $058E's neighbours) instead of the table
feedback missing 068D-06C2 The device entry tables are found from the descriptors' DD_TAB words ($04EE = $468D, $04FF = $46A7: page-1 addresses of this page); the proposals had fragments only
feedback missing 04E6-0504 The $48-byte block copied by ldir at $0180 holds RAM code and two device descriptors; the card shows the descriptors as code and the words proposal at $04CE lands on the RAM code's patched operands
feedback wrong 04CE-04D5 Not words: RAM code (ld a,n / out / jp / jp (hl)) whose operands $0180-$01A1 patch
feedback pattern 0907-3B1F The "4 words, each the address of code the walk reached" proposals at $058F, $0907, $0924, $1AD4, $1B88, $1C2F, $2687, $2E13, $2ECF, $2F08, $3489, $34DE, $3B18 are all CALL/JP/CALL cc instructions that did not run in the profile; an unrun CD/C3/Cx nn nn is not a table
feedback missing 2C58-2D40 The command table (counted name, handler word; 0 ends) is read by $2B9E and $2BF6; the proposals saw only six of its names as text and a few bytes, and the hidden entries $2BF0/$2BF7/$2C0D came from the copyright text at $2BBC
feedback missing 0131-0139 ld de,$C131 at $3FCD (then ldir 9) makes a counted text; the listing decodes $0139 ':' into ld a,($F211) and hides the entry at $013A
feedback listing 0000-3FFF Opened the whole page to judge the proposals: the cards' memory lines did not show which code reads $020C, $0366, $09B6, $1000, $1132, $17E1, $1A96, $2229, $24C2, $2553, $2BBC, $2F38, $2F9E, $2FB7, $33B9, $36D4, $3A97, $3B66, $3BDB (all ld rr,nn of an address on this page)
